.TH AUSCULTE 1 "2026-08-01" "senechal" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
ausculte \- examine the estate for health
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ausculte
.br
.B ausculte dead-config
.br
.B ausculte estate-health
.br
.B ausculte no-self-dev
.br
.B ausculte parked
.br
.B ausculte silence
.br
.B ausculte smart-health
.br
.B ausculte verify-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Auscultation is listening to a body for what it is not saying out loud.
.B ausculte
listens to the estate: the machines, the configuration that claims to
describe them, the disks under it, and \- since 2026\-08\-01 \- the
instruments that report on all of it.
.PP
That last inclusion is the one worth stating, because it is what keeps this
verb one clause rather than two. An instrument that maps three world\-states
\- nothing\-there, could\-not\-look, did\-not\-look \- onto a single output
symbol is not a separate subject. It is unhealthy estate machinery, exactly
like a config that names a file which is absent, or a disk reporting a
failing sector. The estate includes its own senses.
.PP
Every subcommand is offline and read\-only. Run
.B ausculte
with no argument for the current list.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B dead-config
Configuration that references something absent.
.TP
.B estate-health
The overall roll\-up across the estate.
.TP
.B no-self-dev
Assert that self\-development stays off where it is required to be off.
.TP
.B parked
Whether a project is parked with its material proven safe \- backed up,
briefed, and certified in that order. Exit 0 means parked and safe.
.TP
.B silence
Mechanisms that cannot tell silence apart from clean. Reports one line per
flagged mechanism, each naming the flag class, the project, and the
mechanism. Exit 8 under
.B \-\-strict
if anything was flagged.
.TP
.B smart-health
SMART disk health.
.TP
.B verify-all
Run every health check at once.
.SH "THE WORD UNWIRED"
.B parked
was called
.B project-unwired
until 2026\-08\-01, and the rename is not cosmetic.
.B silence
reports a flag class also named
.BR [unwired] ,
and the two meant opposite things: here it was the goal state (parked, safe,
certified), there it is a defect (an executable that no crontab, doc, conf,
unit or sibling script names). One word for two world\-states, inside the
verb whose whole purpose is refusing that. The estate\-side name is now
.BR parked ,
which is what the check actually measures; the defect keeps
.BR [unwired] .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Results only, no commentary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Usage summary.
.SH COST
.B ausculte
cannot spend money. It carries no
.B \-\-summon
flag, and no subcommand of it reaches a metered service. Every check is
offline and free.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The check ran and the estate answered.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error; the caller is wrong.
.TP
.B 4
GAP: a named subcommand has no tooling behind it. An unrecognised
subcommand also lands here rather than on 2 \- see
.I GAPS.md
for why that is recorded rather than quietly changed.
.TP
.B 5
BROKEN: an underlying check exited a code its own contract does not define.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND: a domain could not be read. Never reported as "nothing to report".
.TP
.B 8
FLAGS: a check found something. Above 6 on purpose, so that "it found
something" stays distinct from "it fell over". Every subcommand can return
it; the estate checks speak a legacy dialect and this verb translates it
rather than passing it through.
.SH EXAMPLES
The subcommand names alone, which is the machine surface:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ ausculte list
dead-config
estate-health
no-self-dev
parked
silence
smart-health
verify-all
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I GAPS.md
What this verb names and its tooling cannot yet do.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUSCULTE_LEGACY_ROOT
The checkout holding the estate health checks. Defaults to the
.B senechal
working tree.
.TP
.B AUSCULTE_SILENCE_AUDIT
The silence audit this verb fronts. It is
.B ecosim's
implementation and has not moved repositories, so the path is stated here
and overridable rather than guessed.
.SH HISTORY
Parted off from
.B veille
on 2026\-07\-30 \- one noun, many verbs.
.PP
On 2026\-08\-01 the silence audit was united into this verb, Zach\-directed.
It had been coined independently in
.B ecosim
under this same name, which
.BR "command -v" (1)
could not detect because that verb was never installed \- an availability
check that reads
.B PATH
sees installed verbs, not coined ones. The collision was the signal that the
two were one domain.
.SH SEE ALSO
